format — protects: source and documentation retain the shared formatting rules
build — protects: source compiles into runnable packages
release-preparation — protects: release preparation preserves source and chooses the classified target
github-body — protects: published descriptions preserve reviewed content
outward-lint — protects: outward artifacts have conventional shape and redacted vocabulary checks
target-publish — protects: a target branch reaches its remote only from a bound episode, under an operator grant and after the outward lint
target-worktree — protects: target start, selection, recovery and merged teardown keep code separate from launchpad records
vertical — protects: filed intent admission, common restartable vertical, repair lineage, readiness, typed stops and directory identity before effects — needs: outside-sandbox
license-fixtures — protects: source-only publication preserves license and package privacy
publication-fixtures — protects: public editions retain their reviewed source boundaries
backup-intake — protects: private intake survives backup and recovery
launchpad — protects: launchpad export writes only manifest-listed kit files and instance seeds from the scripts' checkout's commit, carries the commit's compiled runtime and the harness bundle the export's own emit writes, refuses a non-empty destination, a dirty pinned input and a local-terms match, and the export passes harness check, activates its first order, emits control Beacons and reserves a Codex writer without package source
beacon-portability — protects: control Beacon leaves keep one build-free home that no script imports from skeleton source or dist, and a copied control plane without the skeleton emits a decodable control Beacon
checkpoint — protects: pending work can be recovered from named checkpoints
worktree — protects: isolated work and intake survive publish and close
worktree-integration — protects: integration preserves recovery, both histories and authored conflicts without lifecycle events
release — protects: reviewed releases publish idempotently from merged main
work-orders-fixtures — protects: work-order lookup and dependencies identify executable work
siblings-fixtures — protects: the registry generator carries each receipt's fields, the kit version from Git and the orders closed between receipts, reads not evidenced where no receipt supplies a field, and refuses a hand-edited entry, a manifest hash that is not the latest receipt's and an undecodable receipt
kernel — protects: domain events and human judgment contracts replay consistently
compiler — protects: supports compile to the intended constraints and harness behavior
skeleton — protects: the local runtime executes work within admitted authority — needs: outside-sandbox
console — protects: operators can inspect current work and recorded evidence
browser-evidence — protects: standalone browser scenarios produce admitted witnesses, replay and recover owned processes — needs: outside-sandbox
adjacent-queue — protects: operator steering controls the next bounded repair
derived-orders — protects: derived work identity, activation, draft filing, allocation recovery and resident restart remain one control contract
portfolio — protects: a preauthorized portfolio derives bounded orders from WO-119 candidates, materializes them through WO-120 and advances the presence curve only after WO-052 changes and WO-054 verifies them — needs: outside-sandbox
codex-continuation — protects: Codex restores only its owned unfinished task after compaction, continues once and yields to recovery controls
authority-grants — protects: workers cannot grant themselves additional authority
